  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Both angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors and angiotensin receptor blockers (ARBs) are recommended as first-line therapy for high blood pressure (hypertension).",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Both angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors and angiotensin receptor blockers (ARBs) are recommended as first-line therapy for high blood pressure (hypertension)"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Effectiveness: Large-scale studies show that ACE inhibitors (such as lisinopril) and ARBs (such as losartan) lower blood pressure and protect the heart and kidneys just as well as each other.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Safety and Side Effects: ARBs generally have a better safety profile with fewer side effects. ACE inhibitors frequently cause a persistent dry cough and carry a risk of angioedema (swelling of the face or throat) due to bradykinin buildup; these side effects are much less common with ARBs .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Current Clinical Preference: Because they provide equal blood pressure control with fewer adverse events, many modern clinical evaluations and health networks suggest preferentially starting with an ARB over an ACE inhibitor. If a patient cannot tolerate an ACE inhibitor due to a cough or side effects, switching to an ARB is the standard approach .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              2,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow down which option might fit your situation:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Are you or a loved one starting a blood pressure medication for the first time , or switching from another drug?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Do you have any underlying conditions like diabetes, kidney disease, or heart failure?"
          }
        ]
      }
